        "title": "Mechanization History - Plow to GPS, Labor Displacement",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Agricultural mechanization is the story of substituting energy (animal, then fossil fuel) and intelligence (GPS, sensors, AI) for human labor. Each wave of mechanization transformed not just agriculture but society — the McCormick reaper freed millions for industrial work; the combine harvester and tractor enabled the massive 20th-century rural-urban migration; precision agriculture is beginning to re-individualize crop management at sub-meter resolution."
